          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.6: Let us investigate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.152,
            0.743,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take a small part of the food items that you tested for the presence of starch in Activity 3.5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.199,
            0.691,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Place each food item on a separate piece of paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.225,
            0.743,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Wrap the paper around the food and press it. Be careful not to tear the paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.271,
            0.743,
            0.312
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If a food item contains a little water, allow the paper to dry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.317,
            0.744,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does the paper develop an oily patch? What do you think is the reason for this patch? If oil or butter is present in the food item, it leaves an oily patch on the paper. Now, hold the paper against light. Can you see the light faintly shining through this patch? An oily patch on the paper shows that the food item contains fat. Which of these items contain fats? Record your observations in Table 3.3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.484,
            0.373,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3.3.3 Test for proteins"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.518,
            0.446,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.7: Let us investigate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.55,
            0.65,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This activity may be demonstrated by the teacher."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.576,
            0.672,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take the food items tested in previous activities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.603,
            0.743,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Make a paste or powder of the food item using pestle and mortar (Fig. 3.8)."
